# FTQ-002-X5: SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE path collision risk downstream of FTQ-001
#
# Sweep notes:
#   - Pattern SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE|HashMap.*PathBuf in atm-runtime-test-support/src/lib.rs.
#   - pX-s1: open — SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE present at lines 13 and 65;
#     cache uses PathBuf keys derived from OnceLock<Mutex<Option<PathBuf>>> (no env,
#     but same cache-key collision risk when env is added in later branches).
#   - pX-s2, pX-s3, pX-s4: CRATE_ABSENT — absent.
#   - pX-s5: open — SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE present at lines 13 and 63;
#     here env var controls the path and env mutation lacks env_lock (per FTQ-001),
#     so the cache key can diverge across test processes.
#   - integrate/phase-X: CRATE_ABSENT — absent.
#   - Downstream relationship to FTQ-001: fixing env_lock in pX-s5 reduces the window
#     but does not eliminate the HashMap<PathBuf, ...> key-sharing risk entirely.
#     Separate fix required to scope the cache or use a per-test isolation strategy.

<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-002-X5>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-002-X5" ;
  triage:title "SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE path collision risk downstream of FTQ-001" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-runtime-test-support/src/lib.rs — SQLITE_RUNTIME_CACHE uses HashMap<PathBuf, LocalServiceRuntime> keys derived from the env-var-controlled path. When multiple tests share the env var set without env_lock (FTQ-001), the cache can return a runtime from a different test's environment. Present on pX-s1 (lines 13, 65) and pX-s5 (lines 13, 63). Downstream of FTQ-001 env mutation issue; requires its own isolation fix." ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-X" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-14T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-002-X5/pX-s1/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-002-X5/pX-s1/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-002-X5/pX-s5/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-002-X5/pX-s5/2> ;
